# DataFlowBench benchmark-controlled taint-modeling matrix — JavaScript flow
# semantics.
#
# This file is one half of Joern's modeling artifact; the other half is the
# shared adapters/joern/queries/modeling.sc, which carries the source, sink,
# and entry-point declarations. Both are hash-bound into every modeling report.
#
# Syntax is Joern's own textual flow-semantics format:
#
#   "<entity>" <src>-><dst> ...
#
# with 0 the receiver, 1..n the declared parameters, and -1 the return value.
# An entry with no mappings is `NilSemantics` — taint does not leave the entity
# at any position, which is exactly the `sanitizer` role of
# docs/modeling-matrix.md#the-model-declaration-language and exactly the
# explicit no-flow declaration its category-P and category-O negatives ask for.
#
# The quoted key is the declared **member name** rather than a frontend method
# full name. `jssrc2cpg` names a method on an object literal by its inferred
# structural type — `{ carry: (value: ANY) => ANY; block: (value: ANY) => ANY;
# }:carry` — which is a property of the fixture's shape, not of the entity
# being declared. `modeling.sc` therefore re-keys each entry here onto a regex
# over the CPG's method full names. The declaration is unchanged by that: the
# entity identity, the role, and the binding semantics are what this file
# states, and they are the same three parts every other adapter encodes.
#
# Positions here are the declaration language's positions shifted by one,
# because Joern counts the receiver as 0 and DataFlowBench excludes it. So the
# document's `in: 0, out: return` for `Opaque.carry` is `1->-1` below.

# Category P — declared propagators.
# `Opaque.carry`: propagator, in: 0, out: return.
"carry" 1->-1
# `Opaque.block`: the sibling with an identical reflective body, declared as
# explicitly not propagating.
"block"
# `Opaque.select`: propagator, in: 1, out: return. Position 0 is undeclared and
# is not mapped, which is what template 4's negative turns on.
"select" 2->-1

# Category Z — declared sanitizers.
# `Clean.scrub`: sanitizer, in: 0. `Clean.sanitize` is deliberately absent —
# template 6 exists to show that the model binds by entity identity and not by
# a sanitizer-shaped name.
"scrub"

# Category O — opaque procedure summaries.
# `Bridge.pass`: summary, in: 0, out: return.
"pass" 1->-1
# `Bridge.hold`: the sibling carrying an explicit no-flow summary. Its body is
# the identity function, so the body and the summary disagree, which is what
# makes summary activation observable.
"hold"
# `Bridge.deposit`: summary, in: 0, out: 1.payload. Joern's mapping destination
# is the parameter itself; the field discrimination is left to the engine's own
# heap approximation, which is the correct division — the model declares the
# boundary and the analysis decides whether the field separation holds.
"deposit" 1->2

# Category B — persistence boundaries.
# `Store.put`: store-write, in: 1, key: 0 — the value parameter enters the
# store, which Joern addresses as the receiver.
"put" 2->0
# `Store.get`: store-read, out: return, key: 0 — the store leaves through the
# return value. The key and the receiver instance decide whether the roundtrip
# closes, and both are left to the engine.
"get" 0->-1
